\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  As with gladness men of old
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Did the guiding star behold,
\par  As with joy they hailed its light,
\par  Leading onward beaming bright;
\par  So, most gracious Lord, may we
\par  Evermore be led to thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  As with joyful steps they sped,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Saiviour, to thy lowly bed,
\par  There to bend the knee before
\par  Thee, whom heaven and earth adore;
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 So may we with willing feet
\par Ever seek thy mercy-seat.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.   As they offered gifts most rare
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 At thy homely cradle bare;
\par O may we with holy joy,
\par Pure, and free from sin's alloy,
\par All our costliest treasures bring,
\par \pard       Christ, to thee, our heavenly King\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

